  "details": "# Issue\n\nAs it stands, the custom color schemes for VRC+ color all elements of the UI **except** the sidebar buttons in the full menus — These instead take on a *tint* of the button color, and are multiplied, making them dark to almost black.\n\nThis works ***for dark color schemes,*** but directly prevents users from creating \"light\" color schemes (dark text on light background).\n\n# Suggestion\n\nPlease add a \"Light Mode\" toggle for custom themes. The purpose and behaviour of this toggle will be to, when enabled, lighten the darkness of the sidebar button in such a way that darker text may be legible when displayed upon it.\n\nAlternatively, please provide a separate \"Sidebar Text\" color with which users could set independently from the rest of the UI's primary and secondary text.",
